SchemaRecord Specification {#chapter-schemarecord}
=======================================

## Definition ## {#section-schemarecord-definition}

A <dfn>SchemaRecord</dfn> is a [=Record=] that defines a [=Record type=]. A SchemaRecord MUST fulfil all requirements that apply to Records.

The content of a Version of a SchemaRecord is a JSON object in the primary representation (format `application/json`) with the following fields:

<table class="data">
<thead><tr><th>Field<th>Required<th>Type<th>Description</thead>
<tr><td><code>rwpSchemaVersion</code><td>MUST<td>String<td>RWP version for which the schema is valid
<tr><td><code>displayName</code><td>MAY<td>String<td>Human-readable name of the Record type
<tr><td><code>subClassOf</code><td>MAY<td>DID<td>DID with versionHash of the SchemaRecord Version whose Record type this Record type is a subclass of (see [[#section-schemarecord-subclass]])
<tr><td><code>allowedStates</code><td>MUST<td>Array&lt;String&gt;<td>Permitted states of a Version (see [[#subsection-payload-state-model]])
<tr><td><code>stateTransitions</code><td>MAY<td>Array&lt;Object&gt;<td>Permitted transitions between states
<tr><td><code>signaturePolicy</code><td>MAY<td>String<td>One of <code>owner</code>, <code>system</code>, <code>none</code> (see [[#subsection-payload-finalisation]])
<tr><td><code>payloadFormats</code><td>MUST<td>Object<td>Permitted formats per state (see [[#section-payload-format-requirements]])
<tr><td><code>capabilities</code><td>MAY<td>Array&lt;String&gt;<td>Operations applicable to Records of this type (see [[#section-schema-record-capabilities]])
<tr><td><code>jsonSchema</code><td>MUST<td>Object<td>JSON Schema (Draft 2020-12 or later) that validates the content of a Version of a Record of this type
</table>

The `jsonSchema` validates the content of the primary representation of a Version if its format is `application/json`.

<pre class="example json" title="SchemaRecord content (subclass of the Root CaseRecord)">
{
  "rwpSchemaVersion": "0.1",
  "displayName": "Building Permit Case",
  "allowedStates": ["draft", "finalized"],
  "payloadFormats": {
    "draft": ["application/json"],
    "finalized": ["application/json"]
  },
  "jsonSchema": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "type": "object",
    "required": ["title", "trigger", "result"],
    "properties": {
      "trigger": { "minItems": 1, "maxItems": 1 },
      "result":  { "minItems": 1 },
      "parcelNumber": { "type": "string" }
    }
  }
}
</pre>


## Taxonomy ## {#section-schemarecord-taxonomy}

<pre class="highlight language-text">
@prefix rw: &lt;https://w3id.org/recordweb/ontology#&gt; .
rw:SchemaRecord
  rdfs:subClassOf rw:SystemRecord .
</pre>

The Record type defined by a SchemaRecord with `subClassOf` is a subclass (`rdfs:subClassOf`) of the Record type defined by the referenced SchemaRecord.


## Root SchemaRecord ## {#section-schemarecord-root}

The <dfn>Root SchemaRecord</dfn> is the SchemaRecord whose `metadata.core.recordType` is its own DID and whose `metadata.core.schemaVersion` is the versionHash of its own Version. Every other SchemaRecord MUST reference the Root SchemaRecord in `metadata.core.recordType`.

A <dfn>Root Schema</dfn> of a Record type is a SchemaRecord that has no `subClassOf`. The Root Schemas of the core Record types are published in [[#annex-a]].


## Subclass ## {#section-schemarecord-subclass}

`subClassOf` MUST be a Hard Link ([[#section-identity-hash]]) to a finalised Version of a SchemaRecord. A SchemaRecord MUST NOT have more than one `subClassOf`.

The sequence of SchemaRecords reached by following `subClassOf` is the <dfn>type chain</dfn> of a Record type. Because `subClassOf` identifies a specific Version by its hash, a type chain cannot contain a cycle.

A Version of a Record MUST validate against the `jsonSchema` of its SchemaRecord and against the `jsonSchema` of every SchemaRecord in the type chain. A SchemaRecord therefore only contains additions to its parent.

A Record is of a Record type T if its `metadata.core.recordType` identifies the SchemaRecord that defines T, or a SchemaRecord whose type chain contains it. SchemaRecords are compared by DID; the versionHash of a `subClassOf` is not part of the type identity ([[#section-identity-hash]]).

Any Version valid under a subclass MUST be valid under its parent. Therefore a SchemaRecord with `subClassOf`

1. MUST NOT remove a state or a transition of the parent, and MAY add states per [[#subsection-payload-state-model]];
2. MUST NOT permit, for any state, a format that the parent does not permit;
3. MUST NOT define a weaker `signaturePolicy` than the parent (`none` &lt; `system` &lt; `owner`);


## Versioning ## {#section-schemarecord-versioning}

When a SchemaRecord is finalised in a new Version:

1. Existing Records that reference an earlier schema Version REMAIN valid.
2. The new Version MUST reference its predecessor in `parents`.
3. A system MUST keep every schema Version that is referenced by a Record or by a `subClassOf` permanently accessible.

A new Version of a SchemaRecord does not change Record types that are subclasses of it, because `subClassOf` identifies a specific Version.


## Capability Declaration ## {#section-schemarecord-capabilities}

The `capabilities` field declares which operations are applicable to Records of the Record type. Each entry is an operation identifier, for example `retrieve`, `compare`, `validate`, `publish`, or a Record-type-specific operation.

The declaration is descriptive. It does not oblige a resolver to implement the operation and does not grant access (see [[#chapter-access-control]]). A resolver MAY use the capabilities to populate the `RWPFunctionRegistry` service entry ([[#section-didoc-service]]). A change to `capabilities` is a change to the SchemaRecord and MUST be made as a new Version.

